§ `11B and 11N. exposing a child; permitting a young person to consume`

`exposure: all elements` MEANS `Exposure Facts` WITH
    `the accused is 21 years of age or older` IS TRUE
    `the accused was in possession of the thing or of drug paraphernalia` IS TRUE
    `the accused knowingly or recklessly left it exposed in a place, or in a refrigerator, cupboard, cabinet, box, chest or other article that is not locked` IS TRUE
    `the accused knew that a child below 16 years of age has, or is likely to have, access to the place or article` IS TRUE
    `the accused permitted a young person to smoke, administer or consume the thing` IS FALSE
    `the accused did not take all reasonable steps to prevent a young person from smoking, administering or consuming the thing` IS FALSE
    `the accused's possession was authorised under this Act` IS FALSE
    `the accused proves that he or she had the psychoactive substance in his or her possession for a legitimate purpose other than human consumption` IS FALSE

